      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/tools/instantiate-harness.jsonld",
      "@type": "cat-harness:Tool",
      "description": "The scripted step of the initiation process (getting-started.bpmn, the repo-conversion skill §4). Reads the harness's declaration at its pin and every `needs`, transitively (a need beside the instance that needs it unless --repo-of says otherwise, at its default branch's tip unless --pin says otherwise, its declaration's name checked), seeds them all into the repository's index.config.json with the consent given (`remote-mount --seed --whole`), sets `site.landing` to the harness, `site.agentRun` and `mountApprovers`, mounts the closure (`remote-mount`: index.lock.json and the .gitignore mounts block), installs it as root workspaces with the hoisted linker, writes the root bootstrap (`.github/cat.ts` and `.github/mount-from-lock.sh` from cat-harness-tools `templates/root-bootstrap/`) and sets the root's `cat` script to `bun .github/cat.ts`, so `bun run cat …` mounts the layers itself on a later fresh clone, re-renders the agent surface from the mounted generators, runs the harness's `instantiate:<harness>` checkout script when a mounted layer declares it, and commits on a branch (default harness/<harness>). Then, unless --local, pushes the branch, provisions gh-pages when absent (`pages-bootstrap --provision`), opens the setup-only PR, runs `prepare:<harness>` when declared (what the site is built from and nobody commits, such as an IG's AST) and renders the branch's preview at gh-pages branches/<branch>/ (`stage-local`); with --local the site is built and composed and nothing is pushed. It imports only node:*, so it runs from a fresh clone of cat-harness-tools before anything is mounted: it lays the platform's own closure, at the pins the repository will mount, into a temporary root to run the mount from. On a repository with nothing mounted yet, run the same file from a fresh clone: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools /tmp/cht && bun run /tmp/cht/scripts/instantiate-harness.ts …`. Two more flags, not declared as ports because no constrained type carries them yet: `--pin <name>=<sha>` pins one instance of the closure, `--repo-of <name>=<owner/repo>` says where a need lives.",
      "install": {
        "none": true
      },
      "invoke": {
        "shell": "bun run cat harness:instantiate"
      },
      "io": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "arg": {
              "flag": "--repo"
            },
            "description": "The checkout to harness: clean, with a GitHub origin. Default: the working directory.",
            "name": "repo",
            "required": false,
            "schema": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/tool-types.schema.json#/$defs/RepoPath"
          },
